<p>China and Pakistan said they had agreed on a five-point initiative to restore peace in the Gulf and wider Middle East after talks in Beijing between Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi and Pakistan’s Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Ishaq Dar on March 31. The plan calls for an immediate end to hostilities, the start of peace talks, protection for civilians and non-military infrastructure, secure shipping lanes, and adherence to the UN Charter. Both governments said dialogue and diplomacy are the only workable path to de-escalation. The proposal came as the war involving Iran entered its fifth week, with several reports describing ongoing US-Israeli bombardment of Iran and rising risks to regional stability. Pakistan has been seeking a larger peacemaking role and used the Beijing meeting to align its diplomacy with China. Both sides also highlighted the conflict’s economic and social costs for developing countries and stressed the need to keep maritime navigation safe, including through the Strait of Hormuz.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/mvRq_6EmAPeb1gGQu2ym-JGvtpi9TPC8gqaeAUVnusRIBgCJqALn8ZJArrAUd1OmC3HTf-MF62ukpAiCHrAxp_QVRoYFah8pByYXHXuVliD4' alt='Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Ishaq Dar meets China’s FM Wang Yi in Beijing, China on March 31.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Containment push: Beyond calling for an immediate ceasefire, the initiative urged &#x27;utmost efforts&#x27; to stop the Iran war from spreading further across the region.</li><li>Civilian utilities: The joint statement specifically named energy, power, and desalination facilities as civilian sites that should not be attacked, underscoring the risk to basic services as well as industry.</li><li>Pakistan outreach: Dar told Wang that Pakistan had recently hosted a quadrilateral meeting in Islamabad with the foreign ministers of Saudi Arabia, Turkiye, and Egypt as part of its broader push for dialogue on the conflict.</li><li>CPEC review: Alongside the regional crisis talks, the two foreign ministers also reviewed bilateral cooperation under CPEC 2.0.</li></ul><blockquote>Dialogue and diplomacy are the only viable option to resolve conflicts. - Foreign Office statement quoted after the Wang Yi-Ishaq Dar meeting</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>China: Wang Yi praised Pakistan’s &#x27;active diplomatic role&#x27; and its efforts to help end the Middle East conflict, according to Pakistan’s Foreign Office account of the Beijing meeting. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987454/chinas-fm-wang-yi-appreciates-pakistans-active-diplomatic-efforts-in-promoting-middle-east-peace-fo'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Dar’s trip to Beijing reflected Islamabad’s effort to win Chinese backing for peacemaking efforts that had shown little sign of gaining traction as the war continued. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/31/pakistan-china-propose-five-part-peace-plan-middle-east'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Joint Chinese-Pakistani position: The initiative said the sovereignty, territorial integrity, national independence, and security of Iran and the Gulf states should be safeguarded as part of any de-escalation effort. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987106/pakistan-china-issue-5-point-initiative-for-restoring-peace-in-middle-east'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1s8vs5g/china_and_pakistan_present_new_iran_deal/'>China and Pakistan present new Iran deal: Ceasefire for opening Hormuz</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/china-pakistan-propose-peace-plan-for-west-asia-call-for-immediate-end-to-hostilities/article70808006.ece'>China, Pakistan propose peace plan for West Asia, call for ‘immediate’ end to hostilities</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/plus/news/china/diplomacy/article/3348601/china-pakistan-five-point-plan-end-iran-war'>China-Pakistan five-point plan to end Iran war</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987454/chinas-fm-wang-yi-appreciates-pakistans-active-diplomatic-efforts-in-promoting-middle-east-peace-fo'>China’s FM Wang Yi appreciates Pakistan’s active diplomatic efforts in promoting Middle East peace: FO</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/31/pakistan-china-propose-five-part-peace-plan-middle-east'>Pakistan and China propose five-part peace plan for Middle East</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/31/no-truth-to-us-iranian-negotiations-irans-fm-tells-al-jazeera'>China and Pakistan releases a five-point peace plan for the Iran war following a meeting between the two countries&#x27; foreign ministers, Wang Yi and Ishaq Dar, respectively. The plan includes a ceasefire and reopening the Strait of Hormuz. (The Guardian)</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>